cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenRoIS in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
title: >-
  OpenRoIS: Open-Source Middleware Implementing the OMG Robotic Interaction
  Service (RoIS) Framework 2.0
abstract: >-
  OpenRoIS is a community-driven open-source middleware that implements the
  OMG Robotic Interaction Service (RoIS) Framework 2.0. It provides a recursive
  engine that realizes the main and sub HRI Engine roles, a five-method
  component contract, a JSON-RPC 2.0 mapping of the five RoIS interfaces over
  WebSocket, a single-source-of-truth type pipeline in which Python models are
  exported to JSON Schema and generated into TypeScript and C# types, client
  SDKs for web and Unity, and a Python adapter SDK with ROS 2 support, so that
  one service application can address physical robots and virtual agents.
authors:
